1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,816
After a Rejection The rejection filled me with dismay I had expected

2
00:00:05,829 --> 00:00:11,895
recognition and imagined a superb result Instead I felt blue then sullen

3
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:16,539
and finally tempted to grumble that the whole process was absurd An

4
00:00:16,553 --> 00:00:21,342
email from my tutor helped console me without offering false praise She

5
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:26,316
suggested that I examine the feedback before deciding it was unfair A

6
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:31,053
grim mood could make every criticism seem dreadful It could also tempt

7
00:00:31,066 --> 00:00:34,908
me to forsake the project or regard one misfortune as permanent doom

8
00:00:35,816 --> 00:00:40,132
Neither response would help me improve I took a day to rest

9
00:00:40,342 --> 00:00:44,961
then returned to the draft Some comments were hard to accept but

10
00:00:44,974 --> 00:00:49,947
several revealed a genuine gap The experience did not suddenly enchant me

11
00:00:49,961 --> 00:00:55,447
or produce rapture It did however teach me to separate disappointment from

12
00:00:55,461 --> 00:01:00,105
judgment Growth often begins with the willingness to remain engaged when the

13
00:01:00,118 --> 00:01:01,697
first outcome is unwelcome
